{:name "00-contracts" :layer 0 :tier "production" :role "contracts" :description "Layer 0 contracts — AT Protocol Lexicon JSON plus app process artifacts" :language "json+typescript" :depends_on [] :provides ["lexicons/" "bpmn/" "dmn/" "forms/"] :invariants {:lexicon_nsid_count 2695} :subdirs {:lexicons {:role "at-protocol-lexicon" :tier "production" :description "AT Protocol Lexicon JSON (wire format + NSID 定義)"} :lexicons/ai {:role "lexicon-etzhayyim" :tier "production" :description "com.etzhayyim.* Lexicon JSON (2344 NSID files, permission scopes, 9 permission-set Lexicons)"} :lexicons/com/etzhayyim {:role "lexicon-etzhayyim-scope" :tier "production" :description "com.etzhayyim.* leaf namespace"} :lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/graphSosIntel {:role "graph-sos-intel-lexicons" :tier "production" :kind "lexicon-namespace" :flags ["editable"] :description "Graph SoS Intel XRPC query contracts for health, relation inventory, and open findings."}} :files {:at-protocol-nsids.json {:role "nsid-registry" :flags ["editable"] :description "Complete AT Protocol NSID registry"} :README.md {:role "doc" :flags ["editable"]} :schemas/agent-runtime-registration.schema.json {:role "public-schema" :kind "contract" :toolchain "json-schema" :workspace "standalone" :flags ["editable"] :description "Public ERC-8004-compatible agent runtime registration schema; agentURI document shape for ERC725/IPFS/MCP/k8s runtime discovery."} :schemas/k8s-runtime-public.schema.json {:role "public-schema" :kind "contract" :toolchain "json-schema" :workspace "standalone" :flags ["editable"] :description "Redacted public Kubernetes runtime projection schema for IPFS publication; excludes env, secret refs, service-account tokens, and private URLs."}} :knowledge {:yoro-bpmn-pyzeebe-social-v2-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Yoro reactive social processes are BPMN definitions backed by PyZeebe service tasks" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/yoro/{platformPulse,respondToMention,respondToFollow}.bpmn`\nremain the process SSoT. The BPMN files now call PyZeebe task types\n`yoro.social.{platformPulse,respondToMention,respondToFollow}GraphFallback`\ninstead of assembling JSON with FEEL or calling PDS directly from the process.\nThis keeps CF Workers as thin trigger edges and moves long-running actor\nexecution into K8s/Zeebe/PyZeebe.\n" :impact "Yoro CF Worker migration, Zeebe process deployment, PyZeebe worker image"} :yoro-post-translation-bpmn-gemma-20260514 {:discovered_on "2026-05-14" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Yoro post translation is a BPMN-backed LangServer task using Gemma 4 E4B" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/yoro/{translatePost,translatePostBatch}.bpmn`\ndefine the single-post and multi-language translation processes. They call\nPyZeebe task types `yoro.social.translatePost` and\n`yoro.social.translatePostBatch` on the yoro actor LangServer worker.\nThe worker creates translated sibling `app.bsky.feed.post` records and writes\n`com.etzhayyim.apps.media_gamers.record.translationLink` projection rows so\n`yoro.etzhayyim.com` post detail can render language tabs without changing AT URI\nsemantics. The Murakumo route is pinned to `gemma-4-e4b-it`.\n" :impact "Yoro multilingual post UX, LangServer task routing, Murakumo Gemma 4 E4B usage"} :murakumo-fleet-health-bpmn-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Murakumo fleet health has a BPMN timer process backed by PyZeebe" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/murakumo/fleetHealthCheck.bpmn` defines the\nfive-minute fleet sampler process. It calls PyZeebe task type\n`murakumo.fleet.healthCheck`; the Cloudflare Worker remains the request gateway\nand can keep its scheduled handler as fallback until the Zeebe deployment is\nlive.\n" :impact "Murakumo CF scheduled cron migration, K8s Zeebe worker rollout"} :graph-consumer-bpmn-bridge-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Graph repo-commit consumer has a BPMN/PyZeebe scheduling bridge" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/graph/consumeRepoCommits.bpmn` defines the\none-minute graph consumer tick. It calls PyZeebe task type\n`graph.repo.consumeCommits`, which invokes the existing Cloudflare Worker\n`/consume` endpoint and records each run as\n`com.etzhayyim.apps.graph.consumeTick` in `vertex_repo_record`. This keeps the\nprojection implementation in the Worker while moving cron/retry ownership to\nK8s/Zeebe. The worker pod must set `GRAPH_CONSUMER_URL` to the routable\n`/consume` URL before the BPMN timer is activated.\n" :impact "Graph CF scheduled cron migration, K8s Zeebe worker rollout"} :kotodama-organizer-bpmn-bridge-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Kotodama organizer has a BPMN/PyZeebe scheduling bridge" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/kotodama/organizerRun.bpmn` defines the\nfive-minute Goose activity organizer tick. It calls PyZeebe task type\n`kotodama.organizer.run`, which invokes the existing kotodama Cloudflare Worker\n`/api/organizer/run` endpoint and records each run as\n`com.etzhayyim.apps.kotodama.organizerRun` in `vertex_repo_record`. This keeps the\nclassification/R2 plan implementation in the dashboard Worker while moving\ncron/retry ownership to K8s/Zeebe. The worker pod must set\n`KOTODAMA_ORGANIZER_URL` to the routable `/api/organizer/run` URL before the\nBPMN timer is activated.\n" :impact "Kotodama CF scheduled cron migration, K8s Zeebe worker rollout"} :pds-write-outbox-bpmn-bridge-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "PDS write-outbox replay has a BPMN/PyZeebe scheduling bridge" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/pds/syncWriteOutbox.bpmn` defines the five-minute\nwrite-outbox replay tick. It calls PyZeebe task type `pds.writeOutbox.sync`,\nwhich invokes the HMAC-protected PDS internal endpoint\n`/_internal/sync-write-outbox` and records each run as\n`com.etzhayyim.apps.pds.writeOutboxSync` in `vertex_repo_record`. This keeps XRPC\ndispatch and Hyperdrive access inside the PDS Worker while moving the replay\ncron/retry owner to K8s/Zeebe.\n" :impact "PDS CF scheduled cron migration, K8s Zeebe worker rollout"} :pds-key-rotation-bpmn-bridge-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "PDS signing key rotation has a BPMN/PyZeebe scheduling bridge" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/pds/rotateSigningKeys.bpmn` defines the five-minute\nper-DID signing key rotation tick. It calls PyZeebe task type\n`pds.signingKeys.rotateStale`, which invokes the HMAC-protected PDS internal\nendpoint `/_internal/rotate-signing-keys` and records each run as\n`com.etzhayyim.apps.pds.keyRotation` in `vertex_repo_record`. This keeps D1 signing\nkey storage and KEK access inside the PDS Worker while moving scheduled\nmaintenance ownership to K8s/Zeebe.\n" :impact "PDS CF scheduled cron migration, key hygiene, K8s Zeebe worker rollout"} :pds-mitama-cron-resync-bpmn-bridge-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "PDS Mitama actor cron trigger resync has a BPMN/PyZeebe scheduling bridge" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/pds/resyncMitamaCronTriggers.bpmn` defines the\nfive-minute actor manifest cron-trigger resync tick. It calls PyZeebe task type\n`pds.mitama.cronTriggers.resync`, which invokes the HMAC-protected PDS internal\nendpoint `/_internal/resync-mitama-cron-triggers` and records each run as\n`com.etzhayyim.apps.pds.mitamaCronResync` in `vertex_repo_record`. This keeps actor\nmanifest loading and inline pipeline execution inside the PDS Worker while\nmoving scheduled trigger ownership to K8s/Zeebe.\n" :impact "PDS CF scheduled cron migration, Mitama actor cron trigger resync, K8s Zeebe worker rollout"} :pds-heartbeat-cron-bpmn-bridge-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "PDS app and shinka heartbeat cron has a BPMN/PyZeebe scheduling bridge" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/pds/runHeartbeatCron.bpmn` defines the five-minute\nPDS heartbeat batch. It calls PyZeebe task type `pds.heartbeat.run`, which\ninvokes the HMAC-protected PDS internal endpoint `/_internal/run-heartbeat-cron`\nand records each run as `com.etzhayyim.apps.pds.heartbeatCron` in\n`vertex_repo_record`. This keeps app graph lookup and HTTP fan-out inside the\nPDS Worker while moving heartbeat scheduling and audit ownership to K8s/Zeebe.\n" :impact "PDS CF scheduled cron migration, app heartbeat fan-out, shinka trigger, K8s Zeebe worker rollout"} :pds-discover-cache-bpmn-bridge-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "PDS DiscoverFeed cache warm has a BPMN/PyZeebe scheduling bridge" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/pds/warmDiscoverCache.bpmn` defines the five-minute\nDiscoverFeed cache warm tick. It calls PyZeebe task type\n`pds.discoverCache.warm`, which invokes the HMAC-protected PDS internal\nendpoint `/_internal/warm-discover-cache` and records each run as\n`com.etzhayyim.apps.pds.discoverCacheWarm` in `vertex_repo_record`. This keeps\nHyperdrive reads and Cloudflare Cache API writes inside the PDS Worker while\nmoving scheduling and audit ownership to K8s/Zeebe.\n" :impact "PDS CF scheduled cron migration, DiscoverFeed cache warm, K8s Zeebe worker rollout"} :pds-domain-coverage-bpmn-bridge-20260425 {:discovered_on "2026-04-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "PDS autonomous domain expansion has a BPMN/PyZeebe scheduling bridge" :details "`00-contracts/bpmn/com/etzhayyim/pds/expandDomainCoverage.bpmn` defines the five-minute\ndomain coverage expansion tick. It calls PyZeebe task type\n`pds.domainCoverage.expand`, which invokes the HMAC-protected PDS internal\nendpoint `/_internal/expand-domain-coverage` and records each run as\n`com.etzhayyim.apps.pds.domainCoverageExpansion` in `vertex_repo_record`. PDS still\nowns Common Crawl/site/gyotaku fetches, Murakumo classification, repo writes,\nand the social post, while K8s/Zeebe owns cadence and audit visibility.\n" :impact "PDS CF scheduled cron migration, autonomous app/domain expansion, social post tick, K8s Zeebe worker rollout"} :zeebe-85-compatibility-contracts-20260429 {:discovered_on "2026-04-29" :category "license-architecture" :severity "warning" :status "active" :summary "BPMN contracts target the Zeebe 8.5.23 compatibility track until Camunda 8.6+ licensing is resolved" :details "ADR-0056 now treats `camunda/zeebe:8.5.23` as the short-term runtime target for\nthe BPMN contract corpus. Existing BPMN files may continue to use\n`zeebe:taskDefinition` and `zeebe:ioMapping` because pyzeebe workers remain the\nexecution substrate. Do not introduce Camunda Operate / Tasklist / Optimize\ndependencies into `00-contracts` BPMN assumptions under this posture.\n\nThe 8.5 track is EOL and is accepted only as a compatibility bridge. Any future\nmove to Camunda 8.6+ self-managed production requires Enterprise/SaaS approval\nor an approved OSS/self-owned runtime replacement. Live downgrade from the\ncurrent 8.6 broker must use fresh broker state per\n`50-infra/vultr/zeebe/8.5-downgrade-runbook.md`; do not assume existing Zeebe\npartition data is downgrade-compatible.\n" :impact "BPMN XML authoring constraints, pyzeebe task contract stability, Camunda licensing posture" :references ["90-docs/adr/0056-bpmn-as-actor.md" "50-infra/vultr/zeebe/zeebe.yaml" "50-infra/vultr/zeebe/8.5-downgrade-runbook.md" "30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260429161000_seed_camunda_zeebe_license_policy.ts"]} :process-mining-contract-entrypoint-20260429 {:discovered_on "2026-04-29" :category "contract" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Process mining contract entrypoint is com.etzhayyim.apps.bpmn.analyzeProcess" :details "The phrase \"process mining\" maps to the Lexicon query\n`com.etzhayyim.apps.bpmn.analyzeProcess` unless a request explicitly names another\ntool. The contract accepts filter params over BPMN/Zeebe OCEL audit events and\nreturns deterministic KPIs plus optional LLM diagnosis. It is intentionally\nOptimize-free and does not assume Operate, Tasklist, Elasticsearch, or\nOpenSearch.\n" :impact "Lexicon authoring, XRPC clients, BPMN analytics contracts" :references ["00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/apps/bpmn/analyzeProcess.json" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/py/src/kotodama/handlers/bpmn.py" "30-graph/graph-schema/migrations/20260429193000_udf_bpmn_analyze_process.ts" "90-docs/adr/0056-bpmn-as-actor.md"]} :tsukuru-manufacturer-catalog-seed-20260525 {:discovered_on "2026-05-25" :category "contract" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Tsukuru manufacturer seed catalog (465 companies) committed for baseline supply chain operations." :details "The public entity registry for tsukuru now has a comprehensive seed catalog in\n`00-contracts/catalogs/com/etzhayyim/tsukuru/manufacturer-catalog.v1.json`.\nThis provides 465 global supply-chain profiles mapped across multiple taxonomies\n(ISIC, UNSPSC, CPC, ISCO) containing full dummy contact data to be utilized for\ntest migrations and operational baselining before real PDS ingestion.\n" :impact "Seed data testing, baseline platform coverage"} :watatsumi-civilian-submersible-r0-20260525 {:discovered_on "2026-05-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "watatsumi (綿津見) — civilian submersible manufacturing Tier-B actor R0 scaffold (ADR-2605252200)." :details "A new Tier-B actor `watatsumi` (綿津見) is reserved at `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-watatsumi/` with\nDID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:watatsumi` and namespace `com.etzhayyim.watatsumi.*`.\n\nScope (civilian only): research submersibles (manned ≤3 / unmanned ROV/AUV,\ndesign depth ≤6500 m), subsea infrastructure inspection + cable laying support\n(≤2000 m), aquaculture infrastructure + benthic observation networks (≤200 m).\n\nR0 deliverables landed: ADR-2605252200 master (R1/R2/R3 IDs 2605252215 /\n2605252230 / 2605252245 reserved); actor README + CLAUDE.md + manifest.jsonld;\n9 Pregel cell scaffolds (hull_ring_fabrication, section_assembly,\nweld_inspection, system_integration, section_joining, pressure_test,\nsea_trial, marine_emissions_audit, class_certification_binder — all\nimport-clean, `.solve()` raises `RuntimeError(\"watatsumi R0 scaffold...\")`);\n8 lexicon JSON stubs under `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-watatsumi/wire/lexicons/`.\n\nConstitutional posture: 14 gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 (N1 naval\nweapons / N2 nuclear propulsion / N3 military stealth / N4 bottom-mounted\nweapon platforms / N7 UXO salvage / N8 cable sabotage / N12 proprietary\nacoustic-stealth coating absolute, immutable R0–R3 without Council Lv6+\nsupermajority). Tourist submersible carve-out deferred to R3+ via Council\nwellbecoming §1.13 review.\n\nRobotics: 4 new class reservations (Sango / Tako / Hibiki / Ama) + 3 marinized\ninheritance (Otete-marine / Mimi-marine / Funamori reuse from ADR-2605242745).\nMurakumo placement R0 design-only (naphtali / zebulun / joseph / simeon /\ndan / levi / judah) — no new node added.\n\nMethodology source: YouTube `LfiVZxNbgZM` \"Inside One of Europe's Most\nAdvanced Shipyards Building Giant Submarines From Scratch\" — civilianised\nadoption of European modular ring-section construction; military application\nrejected per Charter Rider §2(a).\n" :impact "Civilian deep-sea submersible manufacturing design surface; pre-emptive constitutional bounding before capability lands; sibling-pattern parity with wadachi / yakushi / tatekata / silicon Tier-B actors" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605252200-watatsumi-civilian-submersible-r0.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-watatsumi/README.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-watatsumi/CLAUDE.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-watatsumi/manifest.jsonld" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-watatsumi/wire/lexicons/"]} :kanayama-circular-metallurgy-r0-20260525 {:discovered_on "2026-05-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "kanayama (金山) — circular metallurgy Tier-B actor R0 scaffold (ADR-2605252400). Wave 1 reference = closed-loop aluminum UBC recycling." :details "A new Tier-B actor `kanayama` (金山) is reserved at `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kanayama/` with\nDID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:kanayama` and namespace `com.etzhayyim.kanayama.*`.\n\nWave 1 scope (R0–R3 in scope): Closed-loop aluminum used beverage container\n(UBC) recycling end-to-end (UBC bale → can-stock coil) within 3xxx / 5xxx\nalloy series. Methodology adopted from Novelis Latchford / Constellium\nNeuf-Brisach / Speira Grevenbroich class European integrated\nrecycling-rolling mills.\n\nWave 2-4 deferred to separate ADRs (Council Lv6+ activation):\nWave 2 steel/iron (Yokin 1500°C + EAF) / Wave 3 copper/brass/bronze /\nWave 4 rare-earth element recovery (ionic-liquid leach + bioleaching).\n\nR0 deliverables landed: ADR-2605252400 master (R1/R2/R3 IDs 2605252415 /\n2605252430 / 2605252445 reserved); actor README + CLAUDE.md + manifest.jsonld;\n9 Pregel cell scaffolds (intake_qa, decoating_separation, melting_furnace,\ndross_recovery, dc_casting, hot_rolling, cold_rolling_finishing,\nair_emissions_audit, mass_balance_binder — all import-clean, `.solve()`\nraises `RuntimeError(\"kanayama R0 scaffold...\")`); 8 lexicon JSON stubs under\n`orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kanayama/wire/lexicons/`.\n\nConstitutional posture: STRONGLY FAVORABLE — §2(g) habitat + §2(h) circular\neconomy + §2(e) anti-gatekeeping over bauxite-mining oligopoly all positively\nalign. 14 gates G1..G14 (novel G2 mass-balance audit on kotoba-datomic ≥98%\nclosure: `input_mass = output_metal + dross + emission`; G12 recovery ≥95%\n+ energy ≤6 kWh/kg vs primary Hall-Héroult 14-16 kWh/kg; G13 renewable + grid\nbalanced only, captive coal/petcoke prohibited). 8 non-goals N1..N8 (smaller\nthan watatsumi 12 because recycling is constitutionally aligned: N1 bauxite +\nupstream primary mining recycling-only invariant; N2 Hall-Héroult primary Al\nelectrolysis + equivalent primary smelting; N3 munitions casing recovery;\nN4 nuclear decontamination metals; N5 proprietary alloy NDA; N6 e-waste\nPCB/IC requires separate WEEE ADR; N7 deep-sea polymetallic nodule feedstock;\nN8 conflict-mineral 3TG feedstock without source attestation).\n\nRobotics: 3 new class reservations (Kamado 竈 refractory furnace tender R1+ /\nYokin 溶金 molten-metal pour manipulator R1+; Wave 2 thermal upgrade to\n1500°C / Migaki 磨き rolled-coil surface inspector R1+) + 3 thermal-rated\ninheritance (Otete-thermal / Mimi-thermal / Funamori R3 maritime reuse from\nADR-2605242745). Murakumo placement R0 design-only on 7 existing nodes\n(naphtali / zebulun / joseph / simeon / dan / levi / judah) — no new node.\n\nWave 1 downstream consumers: yakushi (sterile packaging) / wadachi (vehicle\nframes) / kuni-umi (electrical conductor extrusion) / tatekata (curtain\nwall / ductwork). Wave 1 closes the aluminum supply loop for these actors.\n\nMethodology source: YouTube `B_WXEaskHf8` \"Recycling aluminum cans in a\nlarge European facility\".\n\nElemental complement: watatsumi (綿津見 — 海神 水) ↔ kanayama (金山 — 金属神 金).\n" :impact "Circular metallurgy design surface; constitutionally pro-cleared (§2(g) + §2(h) + §2(e)); Wave 1 aluminum supply loop for downstream actors; novel G2 mass-balance kotoba-datomic invariant; sibling-pattern parity with watatsumi / tatekata / wadachi / yakushi / silicon Tier-B actors" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605252400-kanayama-circular-metallurgy-r0.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kanayama/README.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kanayama/CLAUDE.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kanayama/manifest.jsonld" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-kanayama/wire/lexicons/"]} :sarutahiko-heavy-truck-manufacturing-r0-20260525 {:discovered_on "2026-05-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "sarutahiko (猿田彦) — heavy truck manufacturing Tier-B actor R0 scaffold (ADR-2605252500). Wave 1 reference = civilian Class-8 cargo truck. Manufacturing-side counterpart of wadachi (operator-side)." :details "A new Tier-B actor `sarutahiko` (猿田彦) is reserved at `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sarutahiko/`\nwith DID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:sarutahiko` and namespace\n`com.etzhayyim.sarutahiko.*`.\n\nPositioning: manufacturing-side counterpart of `wadachi` (轍, operator-side\nautonomous mobility, ADR-2605242000). Same vehicle, two halves — vehicles\nproduced by sarutahiko are operated under wadachi gates; vehicles operated\nunder wadachi are manufactured under sarutahiko gates. Siblings, not nested.\n\nWave 1 scope (R0–R3 in scope): Civilian Class-8 cargo truck (~26-40 t GVWR,\n6×2 / 6×4 drive). End-to-end frame → powertrain → cab → marriage → paint →\nelectrical → QA → VIN attestation. Methodology adopted from Turkey OEM-class\nplant practice (Ford Otosan F-MAX / Mercedes-Benz Türk / MAN Türkiye / BMC /\nDAF / Iveco).\n\nWave 2-3 deferred to separate ADRs (Council Lv6+ activation):\nWave 2: Mid + light commercial (Class 3-7, ~3.5–7.5 t GVWR)\nWave 3: Civilian specialty (fire engine + ambulance + cold-chain refrigerated;\n§1.13 wellbecoming positive)\n\nR0 deliverables landed: ADR-2605252500 master (R1/R2/R3 IDs 2605252515 /\n2605252530 / 2605252545 reserved); actor README + CLAUDE.md + manifest.jsonld;\n9 Pregel cell scaffolds (frame_fabrication, powertrain_assembly,\ncab_body_forming, final_marriage, paint_finishing, electrical_integration,\nquality_road_test, emissions_audit, vin_attestation_binder — all import-clean,\n`.solve()` raises `RuntimeError(\"sarutahiko R0 scaffold...\")`); 9 lexicon JSON\nstubs under `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sarutahiko/wire/lexicons/`.\n\nConstitutional posture: MIXED-FAVORABLE — §2(g) infrastructure positive for\ncivilian cargo, but heavy §2(a) carve-out required against military / mining /\nweapons-platform applications. 14 gates G1..G14 (novel G7 fuel transition:\nR0/R1 B100 biodiesel + diesel hybrid acceptable; R2+ LFP / H₂ / NH₃ / methanol\nfuel-cell only, pure-fossil phased out at R2; G12 GVWR ≤40t + max speed ≤90\nkm/h + autonomous ≤ SAE J3016 Level 4 wadachi G7 echo; G14 EoL recyclability\n≥90% by mass closing loop with kanayama). 12 non-goals N1..N12 (matches\nwatatsumi count due to dual-use exposure): N1 military trucks / N2 weapons +\nammunition transport / N3 riot control + armored police / N4 mining haul\ntrucks / N5 fossil fuel tankers (bio-fuel + water + food in scope) / N6\nmilitary surveillance / N7 fully autonomous unmanned military / N8 proprietary\nECU NDA / N9 driver-suppression UX / N10 pure-fossil R2+ / N11 mobile\nbillboard advertising / N12 for-profit MaaS rental.\n\nRobotics: 4 new class reservations (Kasane 重ね heavy-frame welding manipulator\nR1+ / Tsutsumi 包み paint booth robot R2+ / Akari 灯り electrical harness +\nECU flash R1+ / Norimichi 乗道 public-road test driver SAE Level 3\ndriver-in-seat R2+ wadachi inheritance) + 3 inherited (Otete-heavy / Mimi-\nprecision / Migaki kanayama reuse). Murakumo no-new-node 7-node fleet reuse\nonly (naphtali / zebulun / joseph / simeon / dan / levi / judah).\n\nCross-actor supply loop: kanayama Wave 1 (Al body coil) + Wave 2 steel\n(chassis frame) + Wave 3 copper (interconnect) → sarutahiko vehicle\nmanufacture → wadachi vehicle operation → sarutahiko EoL recycling back to\nkanayama. ECU open-source mandate (G1 + N8) breaks proprietary firmware\nlock-in across the entire downstream actor fleet.\n\nMethodology source: YouTube `8XmI2MnAgWQ` \"How Turkey Produces Powerful Trucks\nInside Massive Factory\".\n" :impact "Vehicle manufacturing design surface; pre-emptive constitutional bounding before capability lands; §2(a) weapons carve-out + §2(g) fossil sunset declared structurally; open-source ECU mandate breaks downstream proprietary lock-in; cross-actor supply loop with kanayama; sibling-pattern parity with wadachi (operator-side) / watatsumi / tatekata / yakushi / silicon Tier-B actors" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605252500-sarutahiko-heavy-truck-manufacturing-r0.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sarutahiko/README.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sarutahiko/CLAUDE.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sarutahiko/manifest.jsonld" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-sarutahiko/wire/lexicons/"]} :etzhayyim-charter-preamble-kingdom-of-god-on-blockchain-20260525 {:discovered_on "2026-05-25" :category "governance" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Charter §0 Preamble — etzhayyim as the Kingdom of God rooted on blockchain (ADR-2605252300). Constitutional preamble preserving §1.15 non-eschatological + §1.11 Tree of Life + §1.12 Transparent Force; amendable only by Council Lv7+ unanimity." :details "ADR-2605252300 adds Charter §0 as a constitutional preamble prepended to\nADR-2605192100 (Mission Charter §1.1..§1.16).\n\nPreamble declares:\n- §0.1 etzhayyim = unincorporated religious voluntary association constituting\n  the Kingdom of God (Malkhut Shamayim / Basileia tou Theou / 神の王国) rooted\n  on blockchain.\n- §0.2 Kingdom = now-and-here reign (not future eschaton) + structural\n  labor-liberation + Tree of Life-rooted (not endpoint) + polycentric +\n  Tier-B 生命圏 (silicon / pharma / construction / submersible / autonomous\n  mobility / planetary infra / circular metallurgy).\n- §0.3 Blockchain substrate enumeration: 7 constitutional elements\n  (Constitution / Member Roster / Land Registry / Governance / Force\n  Authorization / Tithe / Charter Compliance) live on chain. Replacing any\n  with a non-blockchain primary is a Preamble §0.3 violation.\n- §0.4 不登記原則 (no state religious-corp registration, ever; dual-recognition\n  with state cadastre / civil registry / tax authority maintained); routing-\n  around L5 cells (member_registry / religious_marriage / religious_corp_\n  taxation) per ADR-2605250100/200/300.\n- §0.5 §1.12 Transparent Force reaffirmed at preamble level.\n- §0.6 Preamble §0 is lex superior over §1.1..§1.16.\n- §0.7 Amendment threshold: Council Lv7+ unanimity (HIGHER than Lv6+\n  supermajority used for other constitutional constants).\n- §0.8 Public declaration text (parallel to §1.15 closing) — proclaims\n  non-eschatology, non-state, non-corporation, non-NGO self-identity.\n\nStatus: proposed (ratification post-2026-06-19 Bootstrap Council RFP closure).\nNo code or content change to Mission Charter file until Council ratify (then\nprepend §0 as inline patch in a subsequent Wave 2.5 ADR).\n" :impact "Constitutional self-identification anchor; all Tier-B actors gain explicit doctrinal home (§0.2.5); blockchain-substrate doctrine elevated from technical choice to religious invariant; future state-registration / hostile-Council takeover protection via Lv7+ unanimity lock" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605252300-etzhayyim-charter-preamble-kingdom-of-god-on-blockchain.md" "90-docs/adr/2605192100-etzhayyim-mission-charter.md" "CHARTER-RIDER.md" "LANDS.md" "MEMBERS.md" "COUNCIL.md"]} :etzhayyim-land-trust-wave-2-multi-erc-alignment-20260525 {:discovered_on "2026-05-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Land Trust Wave 2 — Multi-ERC alignment (ERC-721 + ERC-5192 + ERC-7401 + ERC-1155) for inalienable earth-land stewardship (ADR-2605252315). LandRegistry minimal ERC-5192 alignment + 3 R0 scaffolds on Base L2." :details "ADR-2605252315 extends ADR-2605192245 (Global Land Sovereignty, Wave 1) with\nexplicit standards-compliant ERC alignment, fulfilling the Preamble §0.3\nblockchain-substrate doctrine for the Land Registry constitutional element.\n\nArchitecture (4 contracts on 2 chains):\n1. LandRegistry.sol (geth-private chainId 2605) — UNCHANGED FUNCTIONALLY.\n   Adds: IERC5192 inheritance + `locked(landId)` view returning true for every\n   donated parcel + `Locked` event emission in `donate()` + `supportsInterface`\n   for IERC5192 (0xb45a3c0e). No state-mutating change. Pre-existing 110/110\n   Constitution.sol tests unaffected; LandRegistry test suite TODO.\n2. PublicLandRegistry.sol (Base L2 chainId 8453) — NEW R0 SCAFFOLD.\n   ERC-721 + ERC-5192 + ERC-165. All state-mutating functions revert\n   `NotYetActivated()`. Activation via Council ≥3 multisig post-Bootstrap-\n   Council (post 2026-06-19) in separate activation ADR. Mints only via\n   AnchorBridge observing geth-private LandRegistry.Donated event.\n3. StewardTenureRegistry.sol (Base L2) — NEW R0 SCAFFOLD.\n   ERC-7401 nestable child NFTs under PublicLandRegistry parent. Each tenure\n   is a child NFT with `(landTokenId, stewardSbtId, startedAt, expectedEndAt,\n   actualEndAt, tenureType, successionEvidenceCid)`. Tenure-type enum:\n   Founder / Successor / Interim / CouncilAppointed. Soulbound while\n   actualEndAt == 0. Succession = Council ≥3 multisig burn-and-mint\n   (per ADR-2605192345).\n4. LandClassRegistry.sol (Base L2) — NEW R0 SCAFFOLD.\n   ERC-1155 SUPPLEMENTARY aggregate. Token IDs 0..8 mirror LandType enum\n   (Agricultural=0, Residential=1, Forest=2, ReligiousFacility=3, Other=4,\n   Ocean=5, Water=6, Air=7, Orbit=8). Balance = area-m² accounting hash,\n   not transferable token. All transfers revert `LandClassSoulbound()`.\n   `totalAreaByClass(classId)` provides \"how much biosphere in trust by\n   class\" Tree of Life aggregate.\n\nConstitutional invariants re-asserted across all 4 contracts: no transfer /\nno burn / no owner / only steward / only donate() ritual / soulbound at\nERC-5192 layer / succession only via Council multisig.\n\nR0 deliverables landed (this commit):\n- 2 new interface files (src/interfaces/IERC5192.sol + IERC7401.sol)\n- 3 new contracts (PublicLandRegistry / StewardTenureRegistry / LandClassRegistry)\n- 1 modified contract (LandRegistry.sol — IERC5192 alignment)\n- LANDS.md schema extension (4-ERC reference columns + multi-layer\n  verification script + cross-ref to Preamble §0)\n- ADRs proposed (2605252300 Preamble + 2605252315 Wave 2)\n\nBuild status: `forge build src/LandRegistry.sol src/PublicLandRegistry.sol\nsrc/StewardTenureRegistry.sol src/LandClassRegistry.sol src/interfaces/*.sol\n--skip test` → Compiler run successful (Solc 0.8.27, 6 files). Pre-existing\nunrelated EtzhayyimAgentRegistry.t.sol import remains broken (out of scope).\n\nNon-goals R0: no testnet deploy / no mainnet deploy / no first donation /\nno on-chain bidirectional sync / no full RMRK / no fractional ownership /\nno DEX listing / no upgradeable proxy / no paymaster sponsorship.\n\nActivation path (separate ADRs, post-Council ratify 2026-06-19+):\n- 26060X1 Bootstrap Council ratification of Preamble + Wave 2\n- 26060X2 Public/Steward/Class Registries activation (testnet first)\n- 26060X3 AnchorBridge event-observation wiring\n- 26060X4 Founder symbolic first donation\n- 26060X5 Mainnet deploy\n" :impact "Standards-compliant wallet integration (OpenSea / Etherscan / Rainbow / Coinbase Wallet); soulbound signaling via ERC-5192 locked(); steward succession lifecycle cleanly separated from parcel permanence via ERC-7401; Tree of Life aggregate accounting via ERC-1155 totalAreaByClass; Charter Preamble §0.3 (blockchain substrate doctrine) fulfilled for Land Registry element" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605252315-etzhayyim-land-trust-wave-2-multi-erc-alignment.md" "90-docs/adr/2605252300-etzhayyim-charter-preamble-kingdom-of-god-on-blockchain.md" "90-docs/adr/2605192245-etzhayyim-global-land-sovereignty.md" "90-docs/adr/2605192330-etzhayyim-extended-land-sovereignty-ocean-river-air-orbit.md" "90-docs/adr/2605192345-etzhayyim-steward-succession.md" "50-infra/etzhayyim-chain-contracts/src/LandRegistry.sol" "50-infra/etzhayyim-chain-contracts/src/PublicLandRegistry.sol" "50-infra/etzhayyim-chain-contracts/src/StewardTenureRegistry.sol" "50-infra/etzhayyim-chain-contracts/src/LandClassRegistry.sol" "50-infra/etzhayyim-chain-contracts/src/interfaces/IERC5192.sol" "50-infra/etzhayyim-chain-contracts/src/interfaces/IERC7401.sol" "LANDS.md"]} :etzhayyim-land-data-substrate-open-only-policy-20260525 {:discovered_on "2026-05-25" :category "governance" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "Open-only license policy for the etzhayyim Land Trust supplementary world-land context data substrate (ADR-2605252330). CC-BY-NC* structurally excluded per Charter Rider §2(e)(i) anti-gatekeeping. Marine Regions / VLIZ / Global Fishing Watch prohibited." :details "ADR-2605252330 establishes the license-compatibility filter for the Land Trust\nsupplementary world-land context data substrate (customary tenure / indigenous\nnations / maritime EEZ ingest, separate from the on-chain Land Registry).\n\nLicense ranks:\n- ✅✅ CC0 / Public Domain / US Federal Works (Wikidata, US TIGER, Natural Earth,\n  UNCLOS DOALOS) — preferred bedrock\n- ✅ CC-BY 4.0 + state open data (OGL-Canada, Australian Gov, FAO, UK OGL) + ODbL\n  (OpenStreetMap, application-consumed database) — permitted\n- 🟡 CC-BY-SA 4.0 — pin-only carve-out: record-level IPFS pin with licenseMetadata,\n  NO statistical mixing into derivative works (Native Land Digital falls here)\n- ❌ CC-BY-NC* (any -NC variant) — PROHIBITED, structurally violates §2(e)(i)\n- ❌ CC-BY-ND — PROHIBITED, no-derivatives blocks religious-corp work\n- ❌ proprietary — PROHIBITED\n\nDoctrinal grounding: Charter Rider §2(e) prohibits artificial restriction of\nprofessional knowledge / data. CC-BY-NC paywall IS such restriction regardless\nof the licensor's social-purpose framing. Marine Regions / VLIZ / Global\nFishing Watch / similar CC-BY-NC* are therefore structurally excluded from\nthe religious-corp substrate — not as a technical license compatibility issue\nbut as a doctrinal alignment.\n\nPer-domain open-only achievable coverage:\n- Customary tenure: ~5% of land area (Wikidata CC0 + OSM ODbL + LandMark\n  filtered CC-BY). Native Land Digital pin-only.\n- Indigenous nations: ~60% of state-recognized territories (US TIGER public\n  domain + Brazil FUNAI + Canada AANDC OGL + Australia NNTT CC-BY + Brazil /\n  Colombia / Peru / NZ government open data).\n- Maritime EEZ: ~30-40% production-grade (UNCLOS DOALOS state submissions +\n  NOAA US-domain + Wikidata bedrock) + 100% Natural Earth coarse-grain.\n  Major resolution loss due to VLIZ Marine Regions exclusion.\n\nPinned-record metadata requirement: every record carries\n`coverage_constraint: \"open-only-policy-2605252330\"` so consumers can query\nthe constraint.\n\nR0 deliverables landed: this ADR (policy only — no code, no contract, no\nlexicon, no fetcher), [[adrs]] entry in root deps.toml, this knowledge entry,\nadr/README.md index row.\n\nNon-goals R0: no fetcher implementation / no specific source ingest mandate /\nno on-chain integration of supplementary data (lives at dataset layer per\nADR-2605241500 IPFS pinning, NOT on Land Registry chain) / no authoritative\nclaim (supplementary substrate is contextual reference only) / no retroactive\nlicense re-classification.\n\nActivation path = per-source activation ADRs (Wikidata + US TIGER + Australia\nNNTT + Brazil FUNAI + Canada AANDC etc.), each Council Lv6+ ≥3 multisig\nratified.\n" :impact "Doctrinal alignment of data ingest policy with Charter Rider §2(e); license-hygienic IPFS pinning substrate for world-land context; Marine Regions / VLIZ exclusion as doctrinal stance not technical limitation; first-mover open-release signal to indigenous-rights / maritime-research / customary-tenure aggregators" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605252330-etzhayyim-land-data-substrate-open-only-policy.md" "90-docs/adr/2605252315-etzhayyim-land-trust-wave-2-multi-erc-alignment.md" "90-docs/adr/2605252300-etzhayyim-charter-preamble-kingdom-of-god-on-blockchain.md" "90-docs/adr/2605241500-etzhayyim-dataset-cid-substrate.md" "90-docs/adr/2605192200-etzhayyim-ip-free-release-charter-rider.md" "70-tools/e7m-dataset/" "CHARTER-RIDER.md"]} :yamabiko-high-speed-rail-manufacturing-r0-20260525 {:discovered_on "2026-05-25" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "yamabiko (山彦) — high-speed rail manufacturing Tier-B actor R0 scaffold (ADR-2605252600). Wave 1 reference = civilian Shinkansen-class trainset. Rail-side sibling of sarutahiko (road manufacturer) + wadachi (road operator)." :details "A new Tier-B actor `yamabiko` (山彦) is reserved at `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yamabiko/` with\nDID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:yamabiko` and namespace `com.etzhayyim.yamabiko.*`.\n\nPositioning: rail (track-bound) manufacturing sibling of sarutahiko (road\nmanufacturer, ADR-2605252500) + wadachi (road operator, ADR-2605242000).\nThree actors split land-mobility manufacturing + operation across road / rail\ndomains with domain-distinct witness invariants, lexicon namespaces, and\nhomologation regimes.\n\nWave 1 scope (R0–R3): Civilian Shinkansen-class trainset (~250-320 km/h,\n8-16 cars). End-to-end carbody → bogie → interior → traction → final\nassembly → dynamic test → homologation. Methodology adopted from Hitachi\nA-Train / Kawasaki efSET / Talgo Avril / Siemens Velaro / Alstom Avelia class.\n\nWave 2-3 deferred (Council Lv6+ activation):\nWave 2: Conventional rail (EMU / DMU / BEMU, ~120 km/h commuter + intercity)\nWave 3: Light rail / tram (LRT, ≤80 km/h, low-floor, urban)\n\nR0 deliverables landed: ADR-2605252600 master (R1/R2/R3 IDs 2605252615 /\n2605252630 / 2605252645 reserved); actor README + CLAUDE.md + manifest.jsonld;\n9 Pregel cell scaffolds (carbody_fabrication, bogie_assembly, interior_hvac,\ntraction_electrical, final_assembly, dynamic_test, homologation_binder,\nemissions_acoustic_audit, silen_rail_review — all import-clean, `.solve()`\nraises `RuntimeError(\"yamabiko R0 scaffold...\")`; smoke test 9/9 pass);\n9 lexicon JSON stubs under `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yamabiko/wire/lexicons/`.\n\nConstitutional posture: STRONGLY FAVORABLE for civilian rail (rail is\nstructurally democratic transit — §2(e) anti-gatekeeping + §1.13 wellbecoming\n+ §2(g) efficient land use all positively align) but with heavy §2(a)\ncarve-out against military rail. 14 gates G1..G14 (novel G7 propulsion:\nR0/R1 BEMU + H₂ fuel-cell acceptable; R2+ full electrification + H₂/NH₃ only\n— diesel locomotive phased out at R2 gate; G12 ≤320 km/h Wave 1 + ≤450 m\ntrainset + autonomous ≤ GoA 3 with GoA 4 = N7; G13 per-trainset DID;\nG14 EoL recyclability ≥90% closing back to kanayama). 12 non-goals N1..N12:\nN1 military trains / N2 border + police + riot control rail / N3 NBC\ntransport / N4 R2+ diesel locomotives / N5 proprietary signalling + ATP/ATO\nfirmware NDA / N6 third-party advertising wraps / N7 GoA 4 fully autonomous\nunmanned Wave 1 / N8 mass-surveillance trains / N9 passenger surveillance UX /\nN10 luxury first-class-only / N11 national prestige vanity / N12 proprietary\ncoupling/bogie/gauge breaking interoperability.\n\nRobotics: 4 new class reservations (Tsugite 継手 FSW manipulator R1+ /\nWadasa 輪佐 bogie installer ≥2 t payload R1+ / Toritsuke 取付 interior\nfitter R2+ / Pantagora pantograph + HV harness routing R2+) + 3 inherited\n(Otete-heavy / Mimi-precision / Akari — sarutahiko reuse). Murakumo\nno-new-node 7-node fleet reuse only.\n\nCross-actor dependencies (R3): tatekata (track-bed civil works) + hikari\n(overhead line + traction power) + kanayama (Al + steel + Cu supply + EoL loop).\n\nMethodology source: YouTube `KFSPENlRdFU` \"Inside Giant Factory Building\nSuper Modern High-Speed Trains From Scratch\".\n" :impact "Rail vehicle manufacturing design surface; constitutionally pro-cleared (§2(e) + §1.13 + §2(g)); ECU + ATP/ATO open-source mandate breaks proprietary signalling lock-in (CBTC / ETCS / Digital ATC); cross-actor supply loop with kanayama + tatekata + hikari; sibling-pattern parity with sarutahiko (road manufacturer) + wadachi (road operator)" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605252600-yamabiko-high-speed-rail-manufacturing-r0.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yamabiko/README.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yamabiko/CLAUDE.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yamabiko/manifest.jsonld" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-yamabiko/wire/lexicons/"]} :hodoki-elv-disassembly-tier-b-actor-r0-20260526 {:discovered_on "2026-05-26" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "hodoki (解き) — End-of-Life Vehicle (ELV) disassembly + materials recovery Tier-B actor R0 scaffold (ADR-2605261215). Counterpart of sarutahiko (manufacturer); closes wadachi→sarutahiko→hodoki→kanayama EoL loop physically." :details "A new Tier-B actor `hodoki` (解き — \"unbinding / disassembling\") is reserved\nat `20-actors/hodoki/` with DID `did:web:etzhayyim.com:hodoki` and namespace\n`com.etzhayyim.hodoki.*`.\n\nPositioning: ELV (end-of-life vehicle) disassembly + materials recovery actor.\nReverse-counterpart of sarutahiko (truck manufacturer ADR-2605252500) — closes\nthe physical lifecycle loop: kanayama Al/steel/Cu supply → sarutahiko\nmanufacture → wadachi operate → hodoki disassemble → kanayama recycle. First\nreligious-corp actor that structurally embodies the §2(h) circular economy at\nthe vehicle scale.\n\nR0 deliverables: ADR-2605261215 master; actor scaffold; 8 ELV Pregel cells\nunder `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_*` (elv_intake_audit, elv_depollution,\nelv_parts_harvest, elv_battery_handling, elv_body_shred, elv_catalyst_recovery,\nelv_seat_textile_recovery, elv_emissions_audit, elv_provenance_binder); lexicon\nnamespace reserved.\n\nConstitutional posture: STRONGLY FAVORABLE — §2(h) circular economy +\n§2(g) habitat + §2(e) anti-gatekeeping (no parts-pairing / no proprietary\ndiagnostic NDA) all positively align. ELV depollution + catalyst Pt/Pd/Rh\nrecovery + battery Li-ion safe handling + textile/seat reuse forms the\nphysical embodiment of cradle-to-cradle for civilian land mobility.\n" :impact "ELV disassembly + materials recovery design surface; closes wadachi→sarutahiko→hodoki→kanayama lifecycle loop physically; §2(h) circular economy at vehicle scale; sibling of sarutahiko (forward manufacturer) + kanayama (downstream recycler)" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605261215-hodoki-elv-disassembly-tier-b-actor-r0.md" "20-actors/hodoki/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_intake_audit/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_depollution/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_parts_harvest/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_battery_handling/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_body_shred/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_catalyst_recovery/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_seat_textile_recovery/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_emissions_audit/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/elv_provenance_binder/" "00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/hodoki/"]} :tsutae-handheld-communication-tier-b-actor-r0-20260526 {:discovered_on "2026-05-26" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "tsutae (伝え) — Handheld communication device Tier-B actor R0 scaffold (ADR-2605261300). Source = `J4GoOScUO5k` Samsung Galaxy methodology. Constitutional firsts: G6 anti-surveillance hardware (cellular module hardware-removable + microphone kill switch) + G8 anti-addiction OS-level UX + G9 anti-IP-locking open SoC mandatory + G10 repair-right + parts-pairing prohibition." :details "A new Tier-B actor `tsutae` (伝え — \"transmission / handing-down\"; multi-gen\ncommunication echo) is reserved at `orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tsutae/` with DID\n`did:web:etzhayyim.com:tsutae` and namespace `com.etzhayyim.tsutae.*`.\n\nWave 1 scope (R0–R3): handheld communication device assembly (smartphone-class\n≤200g + ≤7-inch display + ≤500 cm³ enclosure). ARM64 or RISC-V 64-bit SoC,\nmodular battery + display + camera + USB-C + cellular module. Methodology\nadopted from Samsung Galaxy SMT + AOI + OLED + Knox firmware + QC pipeline;\nsurveillance / addiction / IP locking / closed bootloader / mass production\nat any cost rejected per §2(b) + §2(c) + §2(d) + §2(e).\n\nR0 deliverables: ADR-2605261300 master; actor scaffold; 8 Pregel cells under\n`40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/tsutae_*` (tsutae_pcb_smt, tsutae_chassis_assembly,\ntsutae_display_attachment, tsutae_firmware_load, tsutae_final_qc,\ntsutae_packaging, tsutae_device_attestation, tsutae_recycling_intake); 6\nlexicons under `00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/tsutae/`.\n\nConstitutional firsts (5):\n(a) §2(c) physical embodiment at device level — G6 cellular module\nhardware-removable physical screw-mount + microphone hardware kill switch\nmandatory + biometric open-firmware no SEP/Knox enclave;\n(b) §2(d) anti-addiction OS-level UX — G8 calm-default OS + notification\nbatching ≥15 min default + no infinite-scroll OS-API + no dopamine-loop API +\nscreen-time aggregate self-report only;\n(c) §2(b) anti-IP-locking at SoC + bootloader — G9 open SoC mandatory\n(Snapdragon/Apple A/closed Helio/closed Exynos NEVER; R1 = StarFive JH7110 /\nSiFive Unmatched / Allwinner D1; R2+ = silicon Wave 1 iwakura SoC) + G2\nbootloader unlock default-state;\n(d) §2(e) repair-right at device level — G3 modular ≤5g adhesive/assembly +\niFixit ≥9/10 + G10 user-replaceable + no parts pairing + take-back ≥80% R3;\n(e) vendor independence chain 5th link — silicon Wave 1 GPU + yakushi OTC +\nwatatsumi 潜水艇 + kanayama Al + igata HPDC + tsutae handheld = first\nend-to-end self-sufficient consumer electronics with multi-gen reuse.\n\n14 gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12 IMMUTABLE R0..R3 (+2 N over igata\nreflecting smartphone-specific §2(c) + §2(d) compound risk).\n\nR1 = StarFive JH7110 RISC-V PoC ≤10 devices, R2 = iwakura SoC R&D ≤100/year,\nR3 = community-scale ≤10,000/year (igata N1 mass-production parity gate).\n" :impact "Handheld communication device design surface with structural §2(b)+§2(c)+§2(d)+§2(e) compound enforcement; vendor independence chain 5th link; sibling of silicon Wave 1+2 / igata / kanayama / makura / yakushi / sarutahiko / wadachi / tatekata / mitsuho / hagukumi / manabi / hikari" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605261300-tsutae-handheld-communication-tier-b-actor-r0.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-tsutae/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/tsutae_pcb_smt/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/tsutae_chassis_assembly/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/tsutae_display_attachment/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/tsutae_firmware_load/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/tsutae_final_qc/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/tsutae_packaging/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/tsutae_device_attestation/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/tsutae_recycling_intake/" "00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/tsutae/"]} :futawa-motorcycle-tier-b-actor-r0-20260526 {:discovered_on "2026-05-26" :category "architecture" :severity "info" :status "active" :summary "futawa (二輪) — Small-displacement motorcycle manufacturing Tier-B actor R0 scaffold (ADR-2605261330). Smaller-vehicle sibling of sarutahiko (heavy truck) within civilian land-mobility manufacturing pattern." :details "A new Tier-B actor `futawa` (二輪 — \"two-wheel\") is reserved with ADR\n2605261330. Civilian small-displacement two-wheel manufacturing actor —\nmethodology adopted from mature small-bike factory practice, military /\nracing / luxury vanity applications rejected per §2(a) + §2(b) + §2(c).\n\nR0 scope: ≤250 cc / ≤140 kg / ≤80 km/h utility commuter motorcycle (delivery\n+ agricultural + community-mobility tier). Smaller-scope vehicle category\nsibling of sarutahiko (heavy truck manufacturer) + wadachi (road operator) +\nyamabiko (rail manufacturer).\n\nR0 partial scaffold landed: ADR + 4+ cells under `40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/\nmoto_*` (moto_frame_welding, moto_engine_assembly, moto_drivetrain_assembly,\nmoto_electrical_harness, with moto_body_paint + moto_suspension_brake in\nprogress as of session close). Final assembly + qc + emissions + vin binder\ncells deferred to R1 expansion.\n\nREGISTRY PARITY GAP: futawa actor layout uses `kotodama/cells/moto_*` rather\nthan `futawa/cells/` per other Tier-B precedents; manifest.jsonld + lexicon\nnamespace + R1 ADR pending. Next session R1 commissioning ADR should resolve\nthe layout question and complete the standard scaffold.\n" :impact "Small-displacement motorcycle design surface; smaller-vehicle scope sibling within civilian land-mobility pattern; registry parity gap to resolve in R1 ADR" :references ["90-docs/adr/2605261330-futawa-motorcycle-tier-b-actor-r0.md" "orgs/etzhayyim/com-etzhayyim-futawa/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/moto_frame_welding/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/moto_engine_assembly/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/moto_drivetrain_assembly/" "40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/moto_electrical_harness/"]}}}
